WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.399 --> 00:00:04.000
There's a lot more to Wong than meets the
eye - even the mystical third eye.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.250
Far from a simple magician's assistant, he's
been an orphan, a lover, and even a doctor

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:09.250
himself.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:13.480
Join us as we break down the history of the
most loyal sidekick of the Sorcerer Supreme.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:19.040
Wong was introduced alongside Doctor Strange
in 1963's Strange Tales #110.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:23.420
The duo is strikingly creepy in their first
comic book outing - not evil, exactly, but

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.660
menacing to behold and always draped in shadow.

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:30.430
Strange is explicitly aligned with black magic
and his Greenwich Village lair is creepy and

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.430
murky.

00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:34.580
Wong first appears when he opens the front
door of Strange's sanctum to a young man in

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:38.730
search of Strange's brand of help, inviting
the guest in with the odd declaration of "Doctor

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:40.110
Strange knows all!"

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:43.030
Wong wasn't a character early on so much as
a piece of set dressing.

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:47.160
He guided people to Strange's office, wore
whatever the artists thought looked "foreign"

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:51.030
enough, and served as a visual reminder of
Strange's ties to the mysterious knowledge

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:52.030
of Asia.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:55.960
As was unfortunately common at the time, this
amounted to whatever mumbo-jumbo the writers

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:57.140
thought sounded convincing.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:02.120
It wasn't until Strange Tales #119 that the
character even got a name.

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:03.160
"And you are?"

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.000
"Wong.”

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.360
“Wong?

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:06.880
Just Wong?

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:07.920
Like…

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.320
Adele?"

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:14.990
Things would change as the decades wound on,
however, and readers demanded better representation

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.440
and more complex stories.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:21.070
Wong's ancestors have served the masters of
the mystic arts for untold generations, with

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:24.470
the family having a close relationship to
the Ancient One in particular.

00:01:24.470 --> 00:01:28.390
Wong was still a baby when he was first presented
to the Ancient One, and was swiftly sent to

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:30.850
ensconce himself in studies of the arcane.

00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:35.409
Wong is particularly tied to a figure named
Kan, his ancestor who lived one thousand years

00:01:35.409 --> 00:01:36.409
ago.

00:01:36.409 --> 00:01:39.909
A student of magic and a brilliant warrior,
Kan was the first to dedicate himself to the

00:01:39.909 --> 00:01:40.909
Ancient One.

00:01:40.909 --> 00:01:44.280
Given that Wong serves Strange and not the
Ancient One, he is the first to break this

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:45.280
tradition.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:49.070
Since the Ancient One commanded this, it's
not exactly a transgression, but it does highlight

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:50.070
Wong's significance.

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:53.720
He's the first person in his family to break
course in centuries.

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:57.920
Though Wong might come from a long line of
warrior-monks singularly devoted to their

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:00.150
duty, he's made time for the ladies over the
years.

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:02.960
Chief among them is Imei Chang, his betrothed.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:05.979
Years passed from the time they were first
engaged, during which they knew they were

00:02:05.979 --> 00:02:09.789
promised to each other but were too young
to wed - years in which Wong went on many

00:02:09.789 --> 00:02:12.909
life-changing adventures and met many fascinating
women.

00:02:12.909 --> 00:02:17.530
Sara Wolfe, Strange's secretary, was a particular
temptation: an attraction grows between her

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:21.430
and Wong that he puts a reluctant stop to,
for the sake of his relationship with Imei.

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:25.610
Though he's far from a disloyal lover, he's
definitely sort of a man about town - "town"

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:27.980
here meaning "the entire cosmos and parts
unknown."

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:32.120
He's got a certain je ne sais quoi the ladies
of every dimension simply can't deny.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:36.440
Superhero problem number one is protecting
those close to you - and no one's been around

00:02:36.459 --> 00:02:38.469
Doctor Strange longer than Wong.

00:02:38.469 --> 00:02:41.169
Naturally, this means that Wong has gotten
kidnapped a lot.

00:02:41.169 --> 00:02:45.560
There's the time in the 1970s when the Shadowqueen
captured him and put him in her dungeon.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:49.540
There's the time in the '80s when Urthona
an alien baddie, abducted Wong along with

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:50.739
Strange's entire house.

00:02:50.739 --> 00:02:53.099
This has happened what feels like dozens of
times.

00:02:53.099 --> 00:02:55.750
The bottom line is, he gets taken captive
a lot.

00:02:55.750 --> 00:02:57.909
But in the modern day, he tends to fight back
more.

00:02:57.909 --> 00:03:01.909
Gone is the Wong who must be held in mystical
stasis for his own protection, as Strange

00:03:01.909 --> 00:03:05.730
so often insisted upon back in the Silver
and Bronze Age stories they starred in.

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:08.040
Here to stay is the Wong who gives as good
as he gets.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.959
Generally speaking, where Doctor Strange goes,
so goes Wong.

00:03:11.959 --> 00:03:13.639
But they haven't always gotten along.

00:03:13.639 --> 00:03:17.480
More than once, Strange and Wong have fallen
out, and at times have come close to ending

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:19.140
their partnership altogether.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:23.790
In the mid-1990s, Doctor Strange: Sorcerer
Supreme told a story in which a demon named

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:27.291
Xaos and the evil sorceress Salome turned
Wong against his friend and master.

00:03:27.291 --> 00:03:31.790
The two villains were able to pull off this
act of trickery due to a very real tension

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:35.579
between Strange and Wong over the Doctor's
failure to protect Imei from being killed.

00:03:35.579 --> 00:03:39.669
They used the prospect of resurrecting Imei
to manipulate Wong to try and kill Strange

00:03:39.669 --> 00:03:40.669
on their behalf.

00:03:40.669 --> 00:03:44.799
Though the two ended up reconciling, it was
a moment of truly broken trust between the

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:49.040
duo that took some time to repair - but ultimately
made their relationship stronger.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:52.160
Wong has been around long enough to have faced
a pantheon of foes.

00:03:52.189 --> 00:03:53.189
Cosmic abominations?

00:03:53.189 --> 00:03:54.189
Check.

00:03:54.189 --> 00:03:55.290
Murderous sorceresses?

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:56.409
Been there, done that.

00:03:56.409 --> 00:04:01.519
But in the 2007 miniseries Doctor Strange:
The Oath, Wong faced down a truly formidable

00:04:01.519 --> 00:04:02.519
villain: cancer.

00:04:02.519 --> 00:04:06.389
At first, he tried to hide his diagnosis from
Strange until he'd found someone to take his

00:04:06.389 --> 00:04:09.919
place at the sorcerer's side - but Strange
still discovered the truth.

00:04:09.919 --> 00:04:11.480
The dude is a doctor, after all.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:15.659
Heartbroken at the prospect of losing his
oldest and most trusted friend, Strange embarks

00:04:15.659 --> 00:04:17.859
on a desperate, frantic quest to save him.

00:04:17.859 --> 00:04:22.090
He succeeded in curing him, but Wong's courage
in the face of seemingly-certain death proved

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:25.760
his fealty to Strange, as well as their mission
of service to the greater good.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:30.720
There's no corner of the Marvel universe more,
well, strange than the one Wong occupies,

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:34.490
and the best Doctor Strange creative teams
lean into the mysticism of it all.

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:38.030
Theirs is the comic series that doesn't have
to play by the rules of superheroics.

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:40.250
Their world is magical, and it follows its
own rules.

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:43.990
It's funny, then, that by and large, Wong
is not himself a magic-user.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:47.280
This is very much not the case in the movies,
where Wong wields sigils and scrolls with

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:48.880
the best of them.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:52.520
"Oh!

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.669
UUnnnh.”

00:04:54.669 --> 00:04:58.490
But on the page, with the exception of a few
alternate universe interpretations and special

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:01.419
circumstances, Wong is merely a peak martial
artist.

00:05:01.419 --> 00:05:04.930
He's comfortable with the spells and sayings
of the world Strange occupies, but he does

00:05:04.930 --> 00:05:06.199
not use them himself.

00:05:06.199 --> 00:05:09.919
He stands in contrast to the magic around
him, and as such, acts as a stable pillar

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:11.560
in a shifting and mystical world.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:16.080
Reimaginings are the bread and butter of superhero
comics, but Doctor Strange and Wong have been

00:05:16.091 --> 00:05:20.400
surprisingly absent from Marvel's many alternate
takes - except for the time that Wong was

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:23.090
inspired by Doctor Strange to become a doctor
himself.

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:27.500
In the 2004 limited series Strange, Wong was
reimagined as a Tibetan orphan who had the

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:31.580
good luck to be saved by Stephen Strange,
then a young medical student.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:35.710
Inspired by Strange's act of kindness, Wong
goes on to become an American doctor operating

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:37.340
under the name Stephen Wong.

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:40.180
He becomes a warrior and a sorcerer in his
own right.

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:43.920
Despite all of this, Wong ultimately still
manages to become Strange's servant - though

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:46.669
the story treats this development as a complicated
one.

00:05:46.669 --> 00:05:50.520
It's a powerful, boundary-breaking story that
asks the question: who should be servants

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:51.569
and who should be masters?

00:05:51.569 --> 00:05:53.909
It's up to the reader to decide.

